仮定法現在 | 要求・提案・必要性を表す動詞/形容詞の that節で、動詞が原形になる | require that he submit

基本形 | V that S + 動詞原形 | The manager requested that the report be revised.
意味 | 「Sが〜することを要求/提案/命令する」 | 「彼が提出する」でも submits ではなく submit
注意 | 三単現の -s を付けない | require that he submit / suggest that she attend
注意 | be動詞も原形 be | recommended that the policy be changed

よく出る動詞 | suggest / recommend / require / request / demand / insist / propose / advise / mandate
例文 | The committee recommended that the plan be approved.
例文 | The supervisor requested that all employees attend the training.
例文 | The policy requires that each applicant submit two references.

よく出る形容詞 | essential / important / necessary / imperative / advisable
形 | It is essential that S + 動詞原形
例文 | It is essential that the data be accurate.
例文 | It is important that every employee complete the form.
例文 | It is imperative that the documents be submitted by Friday.

命令・要求動詞 | demand/insist/propose that S + 動詞原形 | suggest that she attend

demand | 強く要求する | The client demanded that the order be delivered immediately.
insist | 強く主張する | The director insisted that the meeting be postponed.
propose | 提案する | She proposed that the budget be increased.
recommend | 推奨する | We recommend that he take the advanced course.
suggest | 提案する | They suggested that the deadline be extended.

TOEIC罠 | suggest that she attends は不可になりやすい | 正: suggest that she attend
TOEIC罠 | require that he submits は不可 | 正: require that he submit
TOEIC罠 | be動詞は is/are ではなく be | 正: require that the form be completed

仮定法過去 | 現在の事実と違う仮定 | If S were..., S would V

基本形 | If S + 過去形, S would/could/might + 動詞原形
be動詞 | were を使うのが正式 | If I were you
意味 | 実際にはそうではないが、もし〜なら
例文 | If the product were available, we would order it immediately.
例文 | If I were responsible for the project, I would revise the schedule.
例文 | If we had more staff, we could finish the work sooner.

TOEIC罠 | 現在の話でも過去形を使う | If I knew the answer, I would tell you.
TOEIC罠 | would の後ろは原形 | would approve / would be / would submit

仮定法過去完了 | 過去の事実と違う仮定 | If S had V-ed, S would have V-ed

基本形 | If S had + 過去分詞, S would/could/might have + 過去分詞
意味 | 実際には過去に起きなかったが、もし起きていたら
例文 | If we had known about the delay, we would have contacted the client.
例文 | If the shipment had arrived earlier, production would have resumed.
例文 | If she had reviewed the contract, she might have noticed the error.

TOEIC罠 | If節は had V-ed | If we had received
TOEIC罠 | 主節は would have V-ed | would have completed
TOEIC罠 | would have + 原形 は不可 | 正: would have completed

混合仮定法 | 過去の出来事が現在に影響 | If S had V-ed, S would V now
例文 | If he had accepted the offer, he would be working in London now.
例文 | If we had invested earlier, we would be in a stronger position now.

分詞構文 | 接続詞+主語+be動詞などを省略した形 | Given the delay

現在分詞 V-ing | 能動・同時・理由 | Considering the cost, we should postpone the project.
過去分詞 V-ed | 受動・条件・理由 | Given the circumstances, the decision was reasonable.
意味 | because / when / if / although などを短くする
例文 | Seeing the error, the manager corrected the report.
= When the manager saw the error, he corrected the report.
例文 | Having completed the inspection, we resumed operations.
= After we had completed the inspection, we resumed operations.
例文 | Given the delay, we should notify the client.
= Because of the delay / Considering the delay
例文 | Designed for beginners, the course is easy to follow.
= Because it is designed for beginners

分詞構文の頻出表現 | Given 名詞 | Given the circumstances
分詞構文の頻出表現 | Considering 名詞 | Considering the cost
分詞構文の頻出表現 | Regarding 名詞 | Regarding your inquiry
分詞構文の頻出表現 | Based on 名詞 | Based on the survey results
分詞構文の頻出表現 | Compared with/to 名詞 | Compared with last year
分詞構文の頻出表現 | Assuming that SV | Assuming that the figures are accurate

TOEIC罠 | 主語一致が必要 | Walking into the room, the manager noticed the error.
悪い例 | Walking into the room, the error was noticed. | エラーが歩いたことになる
TOEIC罠 | V-ingは能動、V-edは受動 | using / used, including / included

Not only の倒置 | Not only が文頭に出ると倒置する | Not only did sales increase, but profits also improved.

通常形 | Sales not only increased but also improved profitability.
倒置形 | Not only did sales increase, but profits also improved.
ルール | Not only + 助動詞/do/does/did/be + 主語 + 動詞
例文 | Not only did the company reduce costs, but it also improved service quality.
例文 | Not only is the software affordable, but it is also easy to use.
例文 | Not only has demand increased, but supply has also become unstable.
例文 | Not only were the documents incomplete, but they were also inaccurate.

TOEIC罠 | 一般動詞なら do/does/did が必要 | Not only did the manager approve the plan
TOEIC罠 | be動詞なら be を前に出す | Not only is the proposal feasible
TOEIC罠 | 完了形なら have/has/had を前に出す | Not only has revenue increased

否定語倒置 | 否定・制限語が文頭に出ると倒置 | Rarely do we receive complaints.

頻出 | rarely / seldom / never / hardly / scarcely / only after / only when / not until / under no circumstances
例文 | Rarely do employees receive such detailed feedback.
例文 | Never has the company faced such a serious problem.
例文 | Only after the payment is confirmed will the order be shipped.
例文 | Not until Monday will the office reopen.
例文 | Under no circumstances should employees share passwords.

Although と though | although は接続詞、though は接続詞にも副詞にもなる

Although | 基本は文頭または文中でSVを導く | Although sales declined, profits remained stable.
Although | カンマ直後に単独副詞として置くのは基本不可 | × Sales declined, although.
though | 文末副詞として使える | Sales declined. Profits remained stable, though.
though | 文中にも置ける | The proposal, though expensive, is practical.
though | 接続詞としても使える | Though sales declined, profits remained stable.

重要 | 「しかしながら」を文末に軽く足すのは although ではなく though
例文 | The plan is costly. It may be effective, though.
例文 | The software is useful. It is rather difficult to install, though.
例文 | The revised schedule is inconvenient. It is manageable, though.

Although の正しい型 | Although SV, SV | Although the deadline is tight, we can complete the project.
Although の正しい型 | SV, although SV | We can complete the project, although the deadline is tight.
Though の副詞型 | SV, though | The deadline is tight. We can complete the project, though.